From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 06:37:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/asahi: g16: Bound a ready job's wait to 1000 ms
 by default

g16_age_ms is 0 by default, so the engine orders its pending jobs by
priority first, and a low-priority client beside a higher-priority one
that always has a job pending is never picked. Run alone for 60 s,
gpubench-stress-vk queue.depth failed at 39.1 s in each of five runs
on 1.1115 (seeds 0, 1, 2, 3 and 0), reporting a queue that completed
nothing for 15 s, and at 39 s in each of five runs on 1.1117.

Make 1000 the default. Any job that has waited 1000 ms then goes before
every job that has not, whatever the priority, equal priorities
included; of two jobs that have waited that long, the longer wait goes
first. The longest wait measured between clients of equal priority was
595 to 912 ms, beside a compute client 64 deep on 1.1088 and 1.1091.
That is a measurement, not a bound: a job of equal priority that waits
longer is reordered too.

On 1.1117 with the word at 1000, queue.depth passed for 60 s and for
120 s on seeds 1, 2 and 3, and 35 jobs in each 60 s run and 71 in each
120 s run were published after they aged; the same 60 s test failed
with the word at 0. The light cells read, in us per submission at 0
and at 1000, two blocks each: render.light 162.35 / 52.65 / 52.00 and
163.05 / 52.80 / 52.55 at 1 / 8 / 64 queued; compute.light 153.85 /
29.75 / 19.00 and 154.15 / 29.50 / 19.20. The heavy cells, fill and
geom moved by 0 to +0.33 %. At 64 queued the rise is +1.06 % for
render and +1.05 % for compute. No job aged during the cells. With the
word set, a pick reads the clock and two stamps of every pending job,
which it does not do at 0.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/params.rs | 11 ++++++-----
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/params.rs b/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/params.rs
index 365944ecae..3e217923fa 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/params.rs
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/asahi/g16/params.rs
@@ -2437,15 +2437,16 @@ pub(crate) fn submit_retire() -> bool {
     "G16: 1 = a submission first retires the commands that completed since the last poll pass, without waiting for the firmware's event, then publishes (default 0: off; runtime 0644)"
 );
 
-/// Storage of `g16_age_ms` (runtime 0644, default 0).
-static AGE_MS: AtomicU32 = AtomicU32::new(0);
+/// Storage of `g16_age_ms` (runtime 0644, default 1000).
+static AGE_MS: AtomicU32 = AtomicU32::new(1000);
 
 /// `g16_age_ms` = N: a ready job that has waited N ms or longer is picked ahead of every job
 /// that has not, whatever the priorities; of two such jobs the one that waited longer goes
 /// first ([`super::age::before`]). The engine otherwise picks by priority alone, so a
 /// low-priority client beside a higher-priority one that always has a job pending is never
-/// picked. A job waits from when it was queued or its queue was last served. 0: off, the
-/// order by priority alone. Read at each pick.
+/// picked. A job waits from when it was queued or its queue was last served. Default 1000,
+/// above the longest wait measured between clients of equal priority. 0: off, the order by
+/// priority alone. Read at each pick.
 pub(crate) fn age_ms() -> u32 {
     AGE_MS.load(Ordering::Relaxed)
 }
@@ -2456,7 +2457,7 @@ pub(crate) fn age_ms() -> u32 {
     AGE_MS_PARM,
     AGE_MS,
     "g16_age_ms",
-    "G16: a ready job that has waited N ms is picked ahead of priority (default 0: off, priority alone; runtime 0644)"
+    "G16: a ready job that has waited N ms is picked ahead of priority (default 1000; 0: off, priority alone; runtime 0644)"
 );
 
 /// Storage of `g16_check_once` (runtime 0644, default 1).
-- 
2.43.0

